  "source_conclusions": [
    "Pinned wgpu 29.0.4 as_hal_mut opens its encoder, enforces raw-only mode, and leaves finish/submit ownership with wgpu. Three pre/raw/post buffers are submitted once in order; no foreign commit/wait/end or safe/raw encoder mixing.",
    "Prebuffer initializes all six native targets and establishes declared usages; output is transitioned for reading in the postbuffer. Exact Metal device, formats, extents, private storage, tracked hazards, and retained command-buffer references are checked before unsafe encoding.",
    "Pure Objective-C scaler association retains native scaler on the raw command buffer. Rust native owner is explicitly non-Send/non-Sync. Completion callback captures only safe wgpu texture owners and leases; deferred wgpu callback storage survives until submission completion and releases identically on abandonment.",
    "Capacity accounts accepted, candidate, and callback-retired target sets before allocation. Three leases bound queued native work. Engine-owned logical texture budget excludes opaque framework memory explicitly.",
    "Failed preparation does not publish selection/live state. History is dirtied before native encode and accepted only after submit; gaps, missing prior state, content/output size changes, fallback and owner replacement reset native history.",
    "Prefer fallback and Require typed refusal remain distinct, with intentional supported pixel-camera bypass. Capacity/interop stay hard errors. Source003 retains one bounded cached set through fallback without releasing its allocation accounting, and resets history; ignored GPU regression checks exact cached texture identity but has not executed.",
    "Current-to-previous pixel motion removes accepted raster jitter; current-only coverage normalizes native output and excludes overlays from native input. SDK conventions and source numerical controls inspected without claiming GPU numerical or image-quality validation.",
    "Opt-in manifests retain existing resolutions; only incant_render existing package dependencies change and objc2-metal-fx 0.3.2 is added. Default portable path remains selected unless explicitly enabled."
  ],
  "findings": [],
  "limits": [
    "Source003 affected checks remain producer-owned and were running during this source review; no duplicate tests performed.",
    "Actual supported MetalFX six-frame native/fallback/reset ownership case remains ignored/pending delegated execution.",
    "No appearance, performance, iOS device, native cooked temporal, full frame timing, or whole renderer acceptance."
  ]
